From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] grt: release a route's unmerged segments after merging them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FastRoute hands a route over as one segment per GCell step, and
mergeSegments merges the straight runs in place, but resize() keeps the
vector's capacity: every routed net held its unmerged size for the rest
of the run. On a design with 194 m of wire and 121 M vias that is on the
order of 15 GB. The merged segments are the same.

Carried in bazel-orfs for OpenROAD#12075, not upstreamed; retires with
the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/grt/src/GlobalRouter.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/grt/src/GlobalRouter.cpp b/src/grt/src/GlobalRouter.cpp
index 572abc4af6..864fdc9263 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/GlobalRouter.cpp
+++ b/src/grt/src/GlobalRouter.cpp
@@ -5214,6 +5214,8 @@ void GlobalRouter::mergeSegments(const std::vector<Pin>& pins, GRoute& route)
   segments[write] = segments[read];
 
   segments.resize(write + 1);
+  // The route arrives with a segment per GCell; keep only the merged ones.
+  segments.shrink_to_fit();
 }
 
 bool GlobalRouter::segmentsConnect(const GSegment& seg0,
